    "field": "Climate impacts on ice sheets",
    "problem": "Although the latest CMIP6 climate models project a greater temperature rise than their CMIP5 predecessors, the subsequent impacts on future Greenland Ice Sheet surface melt and its contribution to sea-level rise were largely unknown.",
    "method": "The paper uses a regional climate model to dynamically downscale ensembles of CMIP5 and CMIP6 global climate model projections, quantifying the future surface mass loss of the Greenland Ice Sheet and its contribution to sea-level rise.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify the future Greenland Ice Sheet's contribution to global sea level rise by downscaling and comparing climate projections from the CMIP5 and CMIP6 model ensembles using a high-resolution regional climate model.",
